the annual consumption of the building using eq. (1) and table1before hdss step execution. the network’s supply and return temperatures, as well as the heat pump’s supplying temperature to prosumer premises, may vary due to uncertainties in the entire energy demands [8,43]. therefore, the net- work’s operational parameters and pipe sizes, detailed in table 9, are also regarded as uncertain inputs to assess their impact on kpis. in this study, uncertainties in the parameters used to calculate ﬁ- nancial metrics over the project lifespan, as listed in table7, were not considered. for instance, the discount rate is not uniformly distributed as higher discount rates diminish the value of the initial investment. adding more parameters would also reduce the framework’s computa- tional eﬃciency. 3.3.1. risk analysis the risks are evaluated with statistical parameters such as data his- togram, probability density function, cumulative density function and quantiles of npv. to calculate pdf an exponential distribution is se- lected as: 𝑓(𝑥;𝜆)= 𝜆𝑒−𝜆𝑥,𝜆=𝑓(𝜇,𝜎), (43) energy & buildings 325 (2024) 114998 11 a.m. chaudhry, g. ghorbaniasl, j. hachez et al. table 8 list of input parameters representing bounded uncertain energy market variations. inputparameter description initialvalue ﬁnalvalue units electricityprice pricevariation, powerpulse 0.15 0.09 eur∕kwh gasprice pricevariation, powerpulse 0.05 0.07 eur∕kwh emissionelectricity carbonintensityfrom electricitymaps 0.02 0.3 kgco2∕kwh co2 penalty ghgemissiontax 0.10 0.40 eur∕kgco2 ashpprice assumedcapacitypriceforindividualbuildingequipment 145 155 eur∕kw gshpprice assumedcapacitypriceforindividualbuildingandnetworksubstation 103 113 eur∕kw btesprice capacitypriceforseasonalstorageasperflexynet 16 18 keur atesprice capacitypriceforseasonalstorageasperflexynet 145 155 eur boilerprice assumedcapacitypriceforindividualbuildingequipment 100 200 eur∕kw trenchprice assumedcapacitypricefornetworkpipes 1 2 keur∕m fig. 6. schematicdiagram