 the wind-pv-load uncertainty when setting the objective deviation factor to 0.1. table 6 lists four typical solutions in the pareto solution set including optimal γ a , optimal γ b , optimal γ c , and optimal compromise solution, where the compromise solution is obtained ac - cording to fuzzy decision theory ( peng et al., 2019 ). table 6 shows that the optimal operating costs in the four scenarios are quite similar, but the robust objectives vary significantly. specifically, since there is con - flicting nature among the three objectives, the pareto optimal solution obtained under considering only one of the objectives optimally is relatively inferior to the other two objectives. by contrast, although none of the objectives of the compromise solution is optimal, each objective is acceptable on the whole, which would be a relatively ideal solution for the decision-maker. figs. 11 – 13 show the scheduling results corresponding to the compromise solution for λ = 0 . 1, respectively. figs. 11 – 13 reveal that during high wind power output periods with low electric and cooling load demand but high heating load, chp unit output decreases and electric boiler is mainly utilized for heating, while electric chiller can meet cooling load demand. electric energy storage is in charging state. during the day with high electrical load but low heating load, excess heat energy is stored in the heat storage. electric storage is in discharge state, chp unit output increases, and electricity is sold to the grid during peak electricity prices to reduce operating costs effectively. fig. 14 shows the fluctuation interval of wind-pv-load corresponding to the compromise solution in each scheduling period when λ = 0 . 1, which is not symmetric and can better reflect the actual uncertain fluctuation situation. table 7 lists the optimal compromise solutions obtained for ies optimal scheduling based on the mocgdt robust model for different objective deviation factors. table 7 shows that as the objective deviation factor increases, the acceptable operating cost in - creases, while the robustness objective obtained is enhanced. this result is consistent with the previous conclusions obtained from the robust scheduling experiments considering only one type of uncertainty. 4.2.3. comparisons with ro and so to validate the superiority of the proposed mocgdt robust model, we compare it with two popular uncertain optimization methods, ro and so. when the objective deviation factor of mocgdt is set to 0.1, table 8 shows the optimiz",no
